Package: proMotif
Type: Package
Title: Promoter-Resolved Transcription-Factor Binding-Site Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Can", "Ozcan", email = "s.canozcan89@gmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Find and rank transcription-factor binding sites in the promoters
    of a gene using JASPAR and HOCOMOCO position weight matrices. For a gene
    symbol and a TF, it retrieves the gene's transcription start sites from
    Ensembl or EPDnew, groups them into promoters, scans each promoter window on
    both strands, and reports every predicted site with its exact genomic
    coordinates, sequence and per-site p-value. Sites are ranked by a binding
    probability that combines motif strength, agreement between the two motif
    databases and public ChIP-seq evidence from ChIP-Atlas (summit proximity
    and the number of supporting experiments), with ChIP-Atlas downloads limited
    to a user-defined data budget. A discovery mode ranks a gene's candidate
    regulators against a genome-wide promoter background, alternative promoters
    can be compared for the TFs that distinguish them, and FANTOM5 CAGE data
    show which promoter is used in which cell type. Includes a Shiny app.
    Reuses the GLproxScape package's Ensembl fetchers and motif-scan
    conventions.
